10-02T12:42:07-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#671)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9cdfe7e9d3e08536fa5926fff5bc8e5c461c2b14\",\"date\":\"2026-10-02T08:50:34-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#670)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"1f6988896e38fc08d2dd0438b096e1083df5ae6e\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T21:14:35-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#669)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a7cc232a2c20b148dd57ef4e6ff0445cc9705727\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T16:41:55-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#668)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"a5d8db496684f693462b46012cbe8d09a10f637a\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T22:44:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"chore: Remove inert Carbon CSS rules from stock management table (#636)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Co-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\",\"authorName\":\"solomonfortune\",\"authorEmail\":\"solomonbuwule@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"47b97df0997479a954a1f8872b349d80ed6a84e7\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T08:20:23-04:00\",\"message\":\"Limit frequency of update-openmrs-deps.yml\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"2d39088cd412327f7f83f01c2f1b03cdc92baa06\",\"date\":\"2026-10-01T07:40:02-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#667)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"86f3a91ce75dd21aa7dbc03bf092e744481188e7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T19:37:42-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#666)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"22cbf8be40d82587d9c9848e59de197377b53240\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T15:37:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#665)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"0a3ad7a542f68707f96f5e66b27b6064501a7a81\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T13:39:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#664)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"12a145551cda444d3c1a79e62699b7735b8dc892\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T19:38:55+03:00\",\"message\":\"(feat) Migrate stock management to workspace v2 (#661)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (feat) Migrate stock management to workspace v2\\n\\nMoves the stock management workspaces from the v1 workspace API to\\nworkspace v2. openmrs-esm-core#1893 removes the v1 API from the framework.\\n\\nroutes.json now declares a stock-management-group overlay group with one\\nwindow per workspace. The windows keep the extra-wide width and the\\nmaximize button the v1 workspaces had. The group uses the default\\napp-wide persistence. A closable group hides the header close button on\\ndesktop and expects the action menu to provide it, and this app has no\\naction menu.\\n\\nEach workspace component now takes Workspace2DefinitionProps, reads its\\nprops from workspaceProps, and renders inside Workspace2. The titles\\nthat callers used to pass as workspaceTitle are now set by the\\nworkspaces themselves, using the same translation keys. Launch sites\\ncall launchWorkspace2, and the two launch helpers no longer take a t\\nargument.\\n\\nThe stock rule form is now a child workspace of the stock item\\nworkspace, opened with launchChildWorkspace from useWorkspace2Context.\\nIt used to replace the stock item form. Now closing it returns to the\\nstock item. After a new stock item is saved, the form relaunches the\\nstock item workspace with the saved item instead of closing and\\nreopening it, because the two v2 calls are async and could race.\\n\\nRemoves the stock-location-form-workspace adapter. It only opened the\\ncreate location modal, which the locations table already opens directly,\\nand nothing launches it.\\n\\nAdds a mockWorkspace2Props test helper to __mocks__ so tests can render\\nworkspaces with the full v2 prop set.\\n\\n* (fix) Revalidate stock management data through the framework's SWR cache\\n\\nhandleMutate called the global `mutate` exported by swr. That function is\\nbound to SWR's default cache. The framework's openmrsComponentDecorator\\nwraps every component in an SWRConfig whose provider is a shared,\\nmodule-level cache, and the useSWR hooks in this app read from that cache.\\nhandleMutate therefore matched no keys, so the table refresh actions and\\nthe revalidation after saves and deletes never refetched anything.\\n\\nReplace handleMutate with a useHandleMutate hook. The hook takes `mutate`\\nfrom useSWRConfig(), which is bound to the cache of the nearest SWRConfig,\\nand returns a function that revalidates every string key starting with the\\ngiven URL. The 16 components that called handleMutate now call the hook\\nand use the returned function. The call sites and URL prefixes are\\nunchanged. The returned function is added to the useCallback dependency\\narrays that reference it.\\n\\nAdd a test for useHandleMutate that renders useSWR under an SWRConfig with\\nits own cache provider and checks that only the matching key is refetched.\\nUpdate the stock items table and stock source delete tests to mock the\\nhook. The delete test now triggers the component's own onConfirmation\\nhandler instead of calling the mock directly.\\n\\n* Drop the redundant revalidate option from useHandleMutate\\n\\nSWR's mutate revalidates matched keys unless revalidate is explicitly false, so passing { revalidate: true } has no effect. The explicit undefined data argument stays, so the call still takes the same path through SWR's mutate.\\n\\n* Revalidate stock rules after saving a rule\\n\\nThe stock rule form is now a child workspace, so the stock item\\nworkspace stays mounted underneath it. Closing the rule form after a\\nsave returned to the Rules tab with the old list, because nothing\\nrevalidated the stock rule query.\\n\\nThe save handler now revalidates every stockmanagement/stockrule key\\nbefore closing. It uses the mutate from useSWRConfig rather than the\\nhandleMutate helper. handleMutate calls the global mutate exported by\\nswr, which is bound to SWR's default cache, while the framework gives\\ndecorated components their own shared cache. So handleMutate doesn't\\nreach the rule list's query.\\n\\n* Use useHandleMutate to revalidate stock rules after saving\\n\\nReplace the inline useSWRConfig().mutate call and its URL-prefix key filter with the useHandleMutate hook from src/utils.ts, which does the same revalidation through the framework's SWR cache. This matches how the rest of the app revalidates after saves and deletes.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"e7e9ddc2688cceb30360b3f5556f15c5c2e41446\",\"date\":\"2026-09-30T08:55:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#663)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7569d23b56381576417983e541345469f49cb6d9\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T17:38:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#660)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"85f2302790137509b44218d00abbedac9f829621\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T16:40:45-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#659)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7186e045f478718e431affea4f0d09a76ee0d779\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T15:38:16-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#658)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"83700e7971dfce2aebd30ce68edae9148f86eb06\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T14:44:05-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#657)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"84f0064d9abbaf4384ff065622a56550de882e49\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T06:41:38-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#656)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"77148056159dfbdb1221a69ee226df4b2c41a7e7\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T05:42:36-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#655)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"dbcf2bdadc7f5869f77f38cd51f8d9115897c685\",\"date\":\"2026-09-29T01:56:47+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Declare react-dom as a peer dependency (#654)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Add react-dom 18.x to peerDependencies in the stock management app.\\n\\nThe app shell provides react-dom through module federation, but the\\nOpenMRS rspack config only shares the dependencies an app lists in\\npeerDependencies. Without react-dom listed there, the app loads the\\ncopy of react-dom bundled into its own build instead of the shell's.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"6508d732cd4af952fd300b3afb03dfcfe674a29a\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T17:57:27-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#653)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"309aa76e18dd98d754a5f5b7053a69123c8a92ae\",\"date\":\"2026-09-28T14:45:03-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#652)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e2d44ffba8c2cc6e6f4e6cdbfd230d48c5e6c623\",\"date\":\"2026-09-27T16:38:17-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#651)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"af242de966bab117016e0823b5f916cf283fac25\",\"date\":\"2026-09-26T17:05:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5863: Add @carbon/react to peerDependencies (#602)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Declare @carbon/react as a 1.x peer and move it from dependencies to devDependencies, so the build tooling shares it with the app shell instead of bundling a separate copy.\",\"authorName\":\"jwnasambu\",\"authorEmail\":\"33891016+jwnasambu@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"52e042356a0ddb0b5051f2d7d42125374c8260b3\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T15:35:58-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#650)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c892c06a16af292a54c4841f32874c356b5e2d80\",\"date\":\"2026-09-25T07:37:45-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#649)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"878d448c3bedba7cd5047181231164abdfad16d3\",\"date\":\"2026-09-24T14:41:38-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#648)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d475d741a6b486ddfe7afe76582c3d0c06c84031\",\"date\":\"2026-09-24T07:38:18-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#647)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"d467fd5cda29d65534c21df831caf089545c274b\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T13:35:51-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#646)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9e3279724daf169cf1a1594e59e287fd26d4e059\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T16:47:19+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5924: Remove unused yup dependency\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Remove yup from dependencies and devDependencies. Stock management uses Zod for form validation and has no Yup imports.\\n\\nUpdate the lockfile to remove yup and its four unused transitive dependencies without changing retained package versions.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"3ef7ca78a89d9509b43be44b6d51f54a92f47bc3\",\"date\":\"2026-09-22T16:39:16+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) O3-5924: Remove unused image annotation dependency (#644)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Remove react-image-annotate, which has been declared since the initial commit but has no source or configuration references.\\n\\nRegenerate the lockfile to remove its unused dependency tree without upgrading retained packages. Keep the debounce ref change separate.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"9556d5a07c6263b485df10dda346f2ec47df5427\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T18:35:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(fix) Use framework modal for stock locations (#630)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"* (fix) Use framework modal for stock locations\\n\\nRegister the create-location dialog with the framework and pass the table refresh callback explicitly. Keep the existing workspace registration as an adapter.\\n\\nConnect the footer submit button to the location form and cover submission and cancellation.\\n\\n* Fix location modal cleanup and list refresh\\n\\nGuard modal disposal so workspace cleanup cannot close the workspace again. Pass the bound FHIR list mutator through the location hooks and use it after creation and for the table refresh action.\\n\\nAdd regression coverage for StrictMode cleanup, external closure, modal dismissal, and refresh callback propagation. All 122 tests, TypeScript, and lint pass.\\n\\n* fix: Keep the location form open when saving fails\\n\\nWait for location creation before closing the modal and disable Save while the request is pending. Keep entered values available for retry and use a simple refresh callback type.\\n\\nAdd regression coverage for pending saves, failed requests, and successful retries. All six focused tests and TypeScript pass.\\n\\n---------\\n\\nCo-authored-by: Nethmi Rodrigo <nethmi@openmrs.org>\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"1654eec1947db428402f9681a018706c3ffb942b\",\"date\":\"2026-09-21T10:40:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#645)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"83e5f2c5062ff7f05aed61bb1bc90e0271e5f6a4\",\"date\":\"2026-09-20T22:23:25+03:00\",\"message\":\"(docs) Fix README license link\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Link to the repository license, including its healthcare disclaimer,\\ninstead of the missing website license page.\\n\",\"authorName\":\"denniskigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"dfe2d0da4a6c8c69d786eacff1e56845dd790b96\",\"date\":\"2026-09-19T12:44:12-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Upgrade to SWR 2.5.1 (#643)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c6518424a9985afabcf51a135bc0c8742b7f5aad\",\"date\":\"2026-09-18T14:45:09-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Switch to using GitHub Actions cache for Actions\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Ian\",\"authorEmail\":\"ian.c.bacher@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"f7204c0cec9e82315ea2613116561db12e02c3a5\",\"date\":\"2026-09-18T14:39:52-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#642)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"a