8:16:26-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#621)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"65cb93243cec437ff7e4fec8605a717dcccf6d83\",\"date\":\"2026-08-29T00:36:51+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Clean build outputs before bundle size comparison (#619)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"c5d5490c40ab41c962b980ced2984379bc81bd56\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T17:13:16-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#620)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2db0cc4673ee98961555384302779fd8d2700347\",\"date\":\"2026-08-28T12:40:50-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#618)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"997e0b4d7703f7d3a6479abcc1f442a6cdd4162a\",\"date\":\"2026-08-27T11:13:08-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#617)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"c9c886b0cdb3a64814ab091f294a41cea34a99c5\",\"date\":\"2026-08-24T14:27:09+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Fix the e2e Dockerfile (#615)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"The nightly frontend image now ships precompressed importmap.json and\\nroutes.registry.json, and its nginx config serves the .br/.gz variants\\nbefore the plain files. The e2e image kept the nightly image's stale\\ncompressed importmap, which points at versioned app directories that\\nthe glob COPY flattens, so e2e runs fail with timeouts.\\n\\nCopy the frontend files with their directory structure intact and\\nremove the stale compressed variants so the freshly assembled\\nimportmap and routes registry are the ones served. Same fix as\\nopenmrs/openmrs-esm-patient-management#2687.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"13c925ca62c57632ab95e8220981ca6f198d0a5e\",\"date\":\"2026-08-21T13:43:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#614)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"7cfd67ec83601118186c1e975eee2f20d0d36e5b\",\"date\":\"2026-08-19T13:41:26-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#613)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"dab817b8114eff6e9c0f8df0065ddc1c9cdb7117\",\"date\":\"2026-08-17T16:42:46-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#612)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9d89a944771d910d37e955b9a8af6fba587a483f\",\"date\":\"2026-08-14T17:41:42-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#611)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3da426808b09e4277209552a1625c567e8484937\",\"date\":\"2026-08-13T16:47:47-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#610)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"e5066b10d3da425d675c1b434b3eba4ec23850fe\",\"date\":\"2026-08-12T18:47:18-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#609)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"08418219a4f8a0ce2b12d42545240b75d44dc6f0\",\"date\":\"2026-08-12T17:48:04-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#608)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"9efca0616539449c10a85df23560acbbbbcafb45\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T15:52:15-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#607)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"5af6a7363460b5703bfd9302cf93beef79ee54bb\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T22:47:58+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Don't update eslint config (#606)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"List the @openmrs packages that actually track the next tag instead of globbing\\nthe whole scope.\\n\\nThe dependency auto-update workflow has failed on every run since\\n@openmrs/eslint-config landed in the root devDependencies. That package only\\npublishes a latest tag, so resolving @openmrs/*@next failed with \\\"Registry\\nfailed to return tag next\\\" and took the whole yarn up down with it.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"bc258af8e39f5377fa36b4c4573ff8b0f6460157\",\"date\":\"2026-08-11T19:13:24+03:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Adopt @openmrs/eslint-config and ESLint 9 (#605)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"Lint config moves to a flat eslint.config.mjs that spreads\\n@openmrs/eslint-config 2.0.0, replacing .eslintrc. eslint moves from 8.57 to\\n^9.39.0 and the --ext flag goes away, since flat config makes it redundant.\\n\\nComparing the effective rule sets before and after, the overlay re-enables\\nwhat this repo enforced and the shared config turns off: triple-slash-reference,\\nno-extra-boolean-cast, no-prototype-builtins, no-unsafe-optional-chaining,\\nno-useless-escape, prefer-const, exhaustive-deps as a warning, and the three\\nrules typescript-eslint v8 split ban-types into.\\n\\nThe previous config applied testing-library's rules to every file rather\\nthan to tests. All 22 still apply to test files, where jest-dom now applies\\ntoo. They no longer apply to the rest of src, where they had nothing to\\nreport: those rules look for render and screen calls.\\n\\nThe shared config adds no-console, which this repo did not have. It found\\nthree console.info calls, two of them logging a caught error. Those are\\nconsole.error now, which is the level they belonged at. The third logs the\\noperation payload in a branch reached when no operation type matched, so it\\nis a console.warn.\\n\\ne2e was never covered by the lint script. It is now, which is where the\\nremaining reports came from: type-only imports made explicit, one blank line,\\nand a Playwright fixture. Fixtures take a callback named use and call it,\\nwhich eslint-plugin-react-hooks reads as React's use hook, so rules-of-hooks\\nis off for e2e.\",\"authorName\":\"Dennis Kigen\",\"authorEmail\":\"kigen.work@gmail.com\"},{\"hash\":\"fe670c4c484265acafa4fbb77ff5c8e09d387bba\",\"date\":\"2026-08-07T14:49:17-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#604)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"b2f236bfb7aff0127b21a86d432e9082a4083011\",\"date\":\"2026-08-06T18:09:16-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update translations from Transifex (#603)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"49692d7a9814d15b30e68f36c180bfc80f08d27f\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T17:56:59-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#601)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"07854526246e764ad1510586311fdc6337379e78\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T10:17:35-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#600)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"3ede24a9fa9885f7e8ccd1a3172f0578e225f630\",\"date\":\"2026-08-05T07:19:11-04:00\",\"message\":\"(chore) Update OpenMRS dependencies (#599)\",\"refs\":\"\",\"body\":\"\",\"authorName\":\"openmrs-bot\",\"authorEmail\":\"infrastructure@openmrs.org\"},{\"hash\":\"2b865741a426733a8361f2c6075e6402a1abd779\",\"date\":\"2026-08-04T19:5